      "text": "# H5 FULL independent native static mechanics\n\n**Static H5 mechanics accepted; zero new findings. No execution release or clock/availability acceptance.** Both complete Perl programs, all13 Python helper bodies, root release/disposition, actual H4 failed audit and the integrated authority/clock/ownership/stdio/control/source paths were reviewed. No Perl/Python subject/helper/schema import/evaluation/syntax/compilecheck, test/build/install/runtime/Git/reviewer/product/gate action occurred. This reviewer is independent of A's H5 authoring.\n\nThe exact143 physical/142 indexed files and mirror,140 flat implementation/three exact exclusions,48 origin copies,5727 external pins and39 regenerated genuine pairs (13 nonempty/26 identity) verify. Complete INPLACE histories H3 1994/native129/root3, H4 current102/static-native100/actual-native110/failure-root3 verify against full byte censuses and exact mirrors. H4 original92 prepared files plus ten explicit actual attempt additions retain their original meanings; no original index repair, copied fresh attempt, old pass or retry. All679 current D4 source hashes including owned4f4f/678 protected, unchanged857 helper4 implementation files, and11 tool realpath/hash identities verify.10329 static integrity/data checks completed with zero mismatch. No new Git tuple or actual source assembly is inferred.\n\nBoth edited Perl statements now express `exec(SAME literal argv) or POSIX::_exit(126)`. Source-only extraction proves the argv list exactly matches H4 after mandatory H4\u2192H5 path inversion; replacing the expression with the old exec-plus-unconditional-fallback statements restores each ENTIRE H4 Perl file byte-for-byte. Successful exec still replaces the child; failed exec reaches126. Parentheses make the existing argument list explicit; no command, environment, extra process, fallback success, warning suppression, stderr filter or accepted-stderr exception is introduced. `use strict` and `use warnings` stay en